<div class="section-label">Conceptual moves</div>
<ul class="concept-list"><li>An event is a spacetime point; observers disagree about coordinates but not causal structure.</li><li>A lightlike path obeys cΔt=±Δx; no boost tips it outside the light cone.</li><li>Length contraction is about measuring both ends at the same time in your frame; simultaneity is the hidden step.</li><li>Twin paradox is not symmetrical globally because only one twin changes inertial frames.</li><li>Conservation still uses total energy and total momentum; rest mass of a composite system can increase after an inelastic collision.</li></ul>
