<section class="double-glass">
<div class="section-label">Conceptual moves</div>
<ul class="concept-list"><li>Fermions exclude; bosons bunch. The ±1 in the denominator is the entire qualitative difference.</li><li>Density of states is the bridge between allowed k-values and thermodynamic integrals.</li><li>Diffusion smooths concentration gradients; drift adds directed motion from a force field.</li><li>Free energy tells what happens at fixed T: systems minimize F, not necessarily U.</li><li>Irreversibility is statistical: overwhelmingly many microstates correspond to higher-entropy macrostates.</li></ul>
</section>
