<div class="section-label">Conceptual moves</div>
<ul class="concept-list"><li>Quarks and leptons are fermions; photons, gluons, W/Z, and Higgs are bosonic field excitations.</li><li>Hadrons are made of quarks: baryons have three quarks; mesons are quark-antiquark pairs.</li><li>Strong force differs from EM because color charge confines; isolated quarks are not observed.</li><li>General relativity treats gravity as geometry: free particles follow geodesics in curved spacetime.</li><li>CMB and Hubble expansion are evidence for a hot dense early universe; Λ controls accelerated expansion.</li></ul>
</section>
